Let me look at the actual MacRoman mapping more carefully. According to the official Apple Macintosh Character Encoding spec:

0xA0-0xFF in MacRoman:
- 0xA0 = ° (degree sign, U+00B0)
- 0xA1 = ¢ (cent, U+00A2)
- 0xA2 = £ (pound, U+00A3)
- 0xA3 = ¤ (currency, U+00A4)
- 0xA4 = ¥ (yen, U+00A5)
- 0xA5 = § (section, U+00A7)
- 0xA6 = ¦ (broken bar, U+00A6)
- 0xA7 = § (section, U+00A7) - actually this is duplicate
- 0xA8 = © (copyright, U+00A9)
- 0xA9 = ª (feminine ordinal, U+00AA)
